    "layers": {
      "type": "ces-stat-proof",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "",
        "heading": "Your Skin Has 5 Layers. Everything You Have Tried Only Reached The First One.",
        "subheading": "",
        "body": "<p>Here is the thing none of those products will tell you. They all stopped at the same place. The surface of your skin. Eye bags don't live there.</p><p>Eye bags don't start at the surface. They start deeper &mdash; in the tissue where fluid builds overnight, where skin gets thinner with age, where the hollow that makes you look tired actually forms.</p><p>Creams sit on top. Serums sit on top. Even the gel patches you have already tried sit on top.</p><p>Your skin is designed to keep things out and it is very good at its job. That is not a quality problem with the products you chose. It is a physics problem. Nothing applied to the surface can cross that barrier.</p><p>That is the only reason nothing has worked. Not because you did not try hard enough. Because everything stopped at the same wall.</p>",
        "image": "",
        "image_position": "below_body",
        "image_alt": "",
        "image_caption": "",
        "callout_label": "Industry Insight",
        "callout_lead": "The global eye cream market is worth",
        "callout_figure": "$2.8B / Year",
        "callout_text": "<p>Built to keep you buying. Not to reach where the problem starts.</p>",
        "callout_source": "",
        "button_label": "",
        "button_link": "#shopify-section-main",
        "color_scheme": "scheme-1",
        "padding_top": 40,
        "padding_bottom": 40
      }
    },
